      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The evaluation of a simple decision aid in the diagnosis of acute abdominal pain shows that plain abdominal x-rays to exclude bowel obstruction can be avoided if less than two of the following symptoms are present: distended abdomen, increased bowel sounds, history of constipation, previous abdominal surgery, age over 50 or vomiting."},
